#!/bin/bash

# tam-launch-screensaver — start the screensaver (tam-screensaver) in a
# fullscreen terminal on every monitor, then give focus back.
#
#   tam-launch-screensaver [force]
#
# force starts it even when the screensaver is switched off (the menu's
# System → Screensaver uses it). Runs in Alacritty, Ghostty, Foot, or Kitty,
# with the window class org.tamlinux.screensaver and the terminal settings in
# ~/.config/tamlinux/screensaver/.
#
# Ported from omarchy 4.0.4 (omarchy-launch-screensaver) for plan 18 R4.12.
# Changed: the class, the settings path, and the screensaver command; the
# missing-command and focused-monitor helpers are inline. The off switch is
# ~/.local/state/tamlinux/toggles/screensaver-off, which the menu's Toggle →
# Screensaver writes through tam-toggle-screensaver (R4.15e).
